1
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:06,167
This room looks like it was on
the receiving end of a tornado!

2
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:10,007
I don't understand how this hole
could be perfectly spherical.

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:11,940
What is going on?

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:16,037
I'm not sure, but the destruction
spreads into the other room, too.

5
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:20,002
It's safe to say Avdol and the
others made contact with the enemy.

6
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:21,290
Here we go!

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,177
Break down this door, Jotaro!

8
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:25,080
We're going in! Roger.

9
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:27,550
Hurrah!

10
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:05,560
I'll catch you later.

11
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:25,717
My pleasure to be able to stay here.

12
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,297
I will live forever.

13
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:30,077
I will continue to walk.

14
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:32,657
I will continue to walk.

15
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:34,637
I will continue to stay.

16
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:36,137
I will continue to stay.

17
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:39,577
I will continue to stay.

18
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:41,977
End of the world.

19
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:43,440
End of the world.

20
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:46,420
That's the memory? Who poo?

21
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:57,368
Hula!

22
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:58,281
Hula! Hula!

23
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,720
All River!

24
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:07,590
Iggy!

25
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:56,800
Polnareff, the blood that stains my
body is Avdol's handiwork, not yours.

26
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,824
My plan was to eradicate you both
simultaneously, but due to Avdol's intervention,

27
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,569
your demise was postponed.

28
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:10,937
Anyone else would have instinctively
saved himself over risking

29
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:14,137
life and limb to come to the
aid of an oblivious comrade.

30
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:17,520
That alone makes him
responsible for my injuries.

31
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,897
He may have been able to injure me,

32
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:23,392
but it'll take far more than
that to send me to the grave.

33
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:26,364
Now I'll set my sights
on the other interlopers.

34
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:28,914
I'll kill them in the name of Lord Dio.

35
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:34,510
Damn it.

36
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:39,485
I told you not to use your stand, Iggy,
but you just had to show off, didn't you?

37
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:41,470
Stupid dog.

38
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,252
Why'd you have to do it?

39
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:44,650
Hulnareff!

40
00:03:44,733 --> 00:03:46,900
As far as Cool Ice was concerned,

41
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:51,121
Iggy was nothing more than a filthy
stray without resolve or pride.

42
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:53,133
But by its very nature,

43
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:55,497
a stand is a manifestation of the soul,

44
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:57,757
and Iggy's had acted of its own volition,

45
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:00,546
with something compelling
it from deep within.

46
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:09,240
His sand...its spirit is gone!

47
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:11,477
How could this have happened?

48
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,620
Damn it!

49
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,860
All that's left is a lifeless husk.

50
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:18,001
The shell of death is in the air.

51
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:21,062
And another life has been
cut short far too soon.

52
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:24,020
Why am I the only one who survived?

53
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:38,400
You're too slow for
your own good, Cool Ice.

54
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:40,053
But you know something?

55
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:41,030
You're right.

56
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:43,277
I had some pretty selfless friends, huh?

57
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:47,184
I was supposed to look out for
Iggy, but instead he saved my ass.

58
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:03,970
Damn it.

59
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,547
How could this be happening?

60
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:10,419
I've only just begun to
realize what he meant to me.

61
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:13,140
This is how it always is.

62
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:15,773
I don't get it until after they're gone.

63
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:20,020
You were a miserable little mutt
from the start, but despite that,

64
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,984
you never failed to find
new ways to impress me.

65
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:27,317
You were a proud bastard who
lived life by your own rules,

66
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:31,341
and we were the ones who mistook
your self-respect as indifference.

67
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:34,040
I told you not to save me.

68
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,080
Dammit, Fleabag!

69
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:39,221
Why'd you have to be so stubborn?

70
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,120
I knew it.

71
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:03,000
I figured out what you are, Cool Ice.

72
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:26,290
Arrgh!

73
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,877
I knew there was something
strange about you.

74
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,078
You're an immortal.

75
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:33,132
Dio somehow found a way to transform you.

76
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:34,870
No!

77
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:43,520
What the hell is this?

78
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:45,680
What's happening to me?

79
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:50,875
Obviously, your precious master made
the changes without your knowledge.

80
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:53,317
He gave you his blood, didn't he?

81
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:56,929
Guess he left out the part about
you turning into a vampire.

82
00:06:57,360 --> 00:07:02,280
You're just like Dio now, a
disgusting soulless vampire.

83
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:04,540
You bastard!

84
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:15,662
Since you're only feeling it now, the change
must have started after I stabbed you.

85
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:16,730
Come on!

86
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:20,037
You made a vow to protect
your lord and master, right?

87
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,517
What are you waiting for?

88
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:22,430
Bring it!

89
00:07:23,220 --> 00:07:24,120
Go on!

90
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:25,280
Do your worst!

91
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:28,300
Hey, what's the hold up,
Cool Ice? I'm waiting!

92
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:30,225
You're not going to defeat me!

93
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,692
Now go to hell, asshole.

94
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:22,320
Ah, I've got to wait.

95
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:24,010
Iggy!

96
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:34,290
Was...

97
00:08:34,373 --> 00:08:35,900
was that my imagination?

98
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:40,620
Or was it really...

99
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:47,000
I don't have time to sit and ponder.

100
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:51,660
All that matters now is making
it upstairs and finding Dio.

101
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:53,440
Morning can wait.

102
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:56,839
I can't fall apart after
everything they sacrificed.

103
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:23,720
Japan, 43 days had passed since Jojo and
the others began their journey to Egypt.

104
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:25,740
Rosa, stop the car.

105
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:27,160
Hit the brakes.

106
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,379
I want to get out.

107
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:31,402
Madame Joestar,

108
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:33,077
I don't mean to overstep,

109
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:35,657
but it's now really the best
time to stop at a sober stand.

110
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:36,570
Well, of course.

111
00:09:36,653 --> 00:09:38,497
I haven't been to Japan in a while.

112
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:41,597
I'd like to grab a quick bite
before visiting my little girl.

113
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:44,621
Hon, would you be a dear
and hold on to my turtle?

114
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,567
Please, Madame, you mustn't.

115
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:50,357
Places such as these are
for common businessmen.

116
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:53,277
Ladies of your pedigree should
only dine at fine restaurants.

117
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:55,517
I'm begging you, Madame,
don't go in there.

118
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,060
Lighten up, Roses.

119
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:59,537
It's so quaint, I just have to record it.

120
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:02,560
Oh, the local flavor is simply to die for.

121
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,548
Oh, this'll be a good shot.

122
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:10,710
Mr.

123
00:10:10,793 --> 00:10:13,540
Roses, judging by the
madame's cavalier attitude,

124
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:16,956
I take it you've not told
her about Holly's condition?

125
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:20,720
Hey, what's the holdup, Roses?

126
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:21,820
Get over here.

127
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,842
Oh, I'm right behind you, madam.

128
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:31,220
No, I haven't uttered a single word.

129
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:35,794
As far as she knows, her daughter is
battling a severe case of pneumonia.

130
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:39,980
I've worked for the Joestar
family for the past 30 years.

131
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:44,877
As for Miss Holly, I've known her since
she was a little girl in grade school.

132
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:45,790
Believe me,

133
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:50,960
I know that I have to tell her the
truth, but I just don't have the heart.

134
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:54,062
Even coming to Japan hasn't
given me the courage.

135
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:55,880
Holly doesn't have long.

136
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:59,866
If she's not saved, she'll likely
die within the next few days.

137
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:02,957
Would you prefer that I
told Madam Joestar, sir?

138
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:04,160
No, thank you.

139
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:07,657
But I've made my bed with the
falsehoods I've told the madam,

140
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:09,387
and now I have to lie in it.

141
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:12,040
I have to be the one to inform her.

142
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:13,930
Tell me,

143
00:11:14,013 --> 00:11:16,417
are you absolutely sure
the curse afflicting

144
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:19,400
Miss Holly will be lifted
if Dio is killed? I am.

145
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:22,180
Dio's demise will end this, trust me.

146
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:27,817
Polly's body is reacting to energy
from something known as a stand.

147
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:31,429
But only people with said stands
can observe the phenomenon.

148
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:35,015
Put simply, Dio's dark energy
is slowly destroying her.

149
00:11:35,380 --> 00:11:37,500
But Madam cannot see the stands.

150
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:42,057
Instead, she'll have to bear witness to
her only daughter in the throes of death.

151
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:45,220
She must know the time
for secrets is over.

152
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:46,730
Yes.

153
00:11:46,813 --> 00:11:47,819
Yes, you're right.

154
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:49,520
There you are, Roses.

155
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:51,017
What are you still doing out here?

156
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:54,260
Instead of sulking around,
come have some curry udon.

157
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:58,840
Please listen, madam.

158
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:00,777
There is something that
I need to tell you.

159
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:01,690
Oh!

160
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:06,457
Oh, I must get some footage of this delightful
little health drink vending machine.

161
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:07,700
Another good shot.

162
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:10,177
Would you like me to get you one, Roses?

163
00:12:10,260 --> 00:12:11,090
Wait!

164
00:12:11,173 --> 00:12:12,577
Madam Joestar, you have to stop this.

165
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:14,697
Despite appearances, those aren't drinks.

166
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:17,140
Madam, please, you have to listen to me.

167
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:18,880
My, what is it?

168
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:23,380
Well, uh, it's about Miss Holly. Oh!

169
00:12:23,860 --> 00:12:26,677
Look at this Japanese
man's unique fashion sense!

170
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,720
Very nice!

171
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:29,620
Hi there, how are you?

172
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:31,721
Give me a big smile if you would!

173
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:33,877
What the hell are you doing, lady?

174
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,607
Who gave you permission
to videotape me, huh?

175
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,517
Please, madam, get in the car.

176
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:40,600
Nice to meet you.

177
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:42,057
Come back here, dammit!

178
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,260
We're not done!

179
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:46,237
I'll be taking that camera
from you before you leave!

180
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,577
Who do you think you are?

181
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:49,457
You're just a damn foreign hag.

182
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:52,577
You're looking to see some
blood today, you rich bitch.

183
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:54,480
All right, that's enough.

184
00:12:54,860 --> 00:12:57,580
I forbid you to lay
another finger on Madam.

185
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:04,437
Madam, you should try learning a
bit more about Japanese culture.

186
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:05,350
Okay.

187
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:10,020
I couldn't do it.

188
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:13,277
I couldn't tell her Miss Holly
only has a few days left.

189
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,777
It would break her heart.

190
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:17,801
And that's the last thing
I would ever want to do.

191
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:35,520
We've almost arrived, and
I still haven't told her.

192
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,722
I can't put this off any longer.

193
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,440
We'll soon be in sight of the Cujo house.

194
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:43,040
She needs to hear this from me.

195
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:49,957
It's okay I know there's
something you want

196
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:53,197
to tell me you don't
need to pretend anymore.

197
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:55,977
I'm well aware of what's
troubling you Roses

198
00:13:56,060 --> 00:13:59,200
my daughter's life is in
grave danger isn't it.

199
00:14:06,460 --> 00:14:09,737
I called Holly from New
York a few times she put

200
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:12,577
on a brave face and
pretended to be cheerful and

201
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:13,490
lively.

202
00:14:13,573 --> 00:14:16,857
She tried her best to convince
me it was only a mild cold.

203
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:18,420
Whenever Joseph phoned,

204
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:21,317
he would tell me his business
trip kept him very busy,

205
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:23,635
but that I had nothing to worry about.

206
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:27,937
But I knew they were keeping
something important from me.

207
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:30,138
Deep down, I knew something terrible

208
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:32,237
was happening to my daughter and husband.

209
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:35,037
I've been married to
Joseph for 50 years now,

210
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:38,020
and my sweet holly is
my own flesh and blood.

211
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:44,117
I never pressed them for more information
because I was afraid of what they'd say.

212
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,837
I wanted nothing more than
to see my precious daughter,

213
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:50,332
but the thought of what I'd
find here was almost too much.

214
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:54,777
You know this much, so you also
have the right to know the rest.

215
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:57,957
As it stands, your daughter only
has a few days left to live.

216
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:58,940
That's why Mr.

217
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:02,817
Joestar and the others went to Egypt
to end the source of her illness.

218
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:05,076
But there's been no news for a while.

219
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:09,935
Please, can you find it in your heart
to forgive me for not telling you?

220
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:12,217
There was nothing we
could do for Miss Holly,

221
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:15,177
so I wanted to spare you from
the pain, but I was wrong.

222
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,357
I should have told you.

223
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:18,100
It was cruel of me not to.

224
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:23,133
I don't want to hear any more
of that foolishness, Roses.

225
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:27,891
No matter how grim things seem, there's
still one thing we can do for Holly.

226
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,580
Hi, sweet girl.

227
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:02,360
I'm so glad you're here.

228
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:05,837
Listen to me very carefully, Roses.

229
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:10,040
Right now, the one thing we can
do for my daughter is have faith.

230
00:16:11,060 --> 00:16:13,517
I don't understand
everything that's happening,

231
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:17,777
but here's what I do know:
Joseph and my grandson, Jotaro,

232
00:16:17,860 --> 00:16:20,697
are putting their lives on
the line in the hope of saving

233
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:24,077
Holly and I believe they will
find a way to do just that.

234
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:28,917
He's never failed me, not once in the
50 years I have known him. He's kept.

235
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,937
every promise he's made since
the two of us met in Italy.

236
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:36,667
Once he's made up his mind to do something,
nothing in this world can stop him.

237
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,569
Rest and believe in
Jotaro and your father.

238
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:45,386
You'll be better before you know it, and
our family will be together once again.

239
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:47,280
Thank you, Mama.

240
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:54,640
Madam Joestar, Miss Holly,
please hang in there.

241
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:13,680
That cool ice, Billy
Jean, even Darby Younger.

242
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:17,320
I knew they were nothing
but incompetent fools.

243
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:30,440
I shouldn't laugh, but knowing they got
what they deserve feels so satisfying!

244
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:35,022
That's what the fools get
for calling me a loser.

245
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:38,300
But at least now we know
I wasn't one after all.

246
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:40,080
Don't be absurd.

247
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:44,057
You can't possibly defeat the
Joestars using that pathetic power.

248
00:17:44,140 --> 00:17:45,434
Out of the way, loser.

249
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,300
Hey, but that's not fair!

250
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:49,540
I want a chance to fight them too!

251
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:52,060
You're merely an ordinary vampire.

252
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:55,817
You'd best stay out of our way
or we might end up killing you.

253
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:58,500
Do try to behave yourself, loser.

254
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:04,400
I'll be the one who finishes off Jotaro!

255
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,470
Stop!

256
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:14,072
There's something up ahead, to the right!

257
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:25,360
A woman!

258
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:27,097
Oh!

259
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:28,920
Please have mercy on me!

260
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:30,340
I'm begging you!

261
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:31,656
Don't suck my blood!

262
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:32,820
Anything but that!

263
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,880
I swear I'll do whatever you want!

264
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:38,120
Just let me live!

265
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:39,574
That's all I'm asking!

266
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:42,600
Hey! Easy now!

267
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:44,194
You need to calm down!

268
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:45,980
I won't run away anymore!

269
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,420
You can trust me!

270
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:48,617
Please have mercy!

271
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:49,530
Just breathe!

272
00:18:49,613 --> 00:18:52,917
We aren't Dio's minions, and
we're certainly not vampires!

273
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:53,997
We're the good guys!

274
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:58,057
So just calm down and
let us help you you're

275
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:03,197
good guys good guys
you're really not those

276
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:05,497
evil vampires you're
actually going to help

277
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:08,920
me get away from here
that's right we're good

278
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:20,877
real good at punching evil in the
face if you still want help we'll be

279
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:25,077
happy to oblige we'll I'll help by
sending you on a one-way trip to hell.

280
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,400
Sound good, Kaku-een?

281
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:31,750
Help!

282
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:34,440
Damn it! Help! Help me! Help!

283
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:37,820
How did you figure it out?

284
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:40,400
My power is impossible to crack!

285
00:19:40,740 --> 00:19:42,597
Would this power have anything to do with

286
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:44,697
the face of a woman on
the back of your head?

287
00:19:44,780 --> 00:19:46,737
For future reference,
when you flip your head,

288
00:19:46,820 --> 00:19:49,349
you should make sure
your hands match, too.

289
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:53,700
Shit! You're right!

290
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:55,020
I never noticed!

291
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:56,160
I'm an idiot!

292
00:19:56,580 --> 00:19:57,900
No, you're a loser.

293
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:00,840
Now where is Dio's room? Out with it.

294
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:03,557
Jotaro, try not to knock him unconscious.

295
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,934
He can take us to Dio.

296
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:07,760
How dare you!

297
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:09,297
Don't you call me that!

298
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:13,145
You're just like those other guys,
so you'll meet the same fate!

299
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:15,140
I'll kill you!

300
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:17,479
Lord Dio's powers made me immortal!

301
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:20,268
And I'll use all of it
to rip you to pieces!

302
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:27,237
So unless I heard wrong, you
just said you were an immortal.

303
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,340
So you're a vampire like Dio.

304
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:31,260
In which case,

305
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:35,597
I can use you as a practice dummy for
when I fight against the real thing.

306
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:36,920
Oh my god!

307
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:41,670
No!

308
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:50,820
So you really are immortal,

309
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:52,197
but vampire or not,

310
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:55,837
we can still rip you into little pieces
and scatter them around the room.

311
00:20:55,920 --> 00:20:58,360
Well, are you taking us to Dio or not?

312
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:00,060
The sun is about to set.

313
00:21:00,540 --> 00:21:04,200
Okay, but can I at
least ask you one thing?

314
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:08,878
How the hell did you know the other
stand users used to call me loser?

315
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:11,720
Oh, man, good grief.

316
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:39,630
Thank you.

317
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:12,460
Thank you.

318
00:22:49,180 --> 00:22:50,640
I gotta hand it to him.

319
00:22:51,180 --> 00:22:53,298
Dio's got some pretty nice curtains.

320
00:22:57,220 --> 00:22:58,050
All right.

321
00:22:58,420 --> 00:23:01,302
Now I can walk and even
jump around if I need to.

322
00:23:01,420 --> 00:23:05,773
It still hurts a bit, but now's not
the time to worry about a little pain.

323
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:16,576
Greetings, Polareff.

324
00:23:16,740 --> 00:23:18,280
What a pleasant surprise.

325
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:22,520
Dio, at last.

326
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:28,620
You've finally come out, Dio.

327
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,500
I knew this day would come.

328
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:32,520
I have absolutely no regrets.

329
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:34,917
There's something you need to hear first.

330
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,577
Is he playing games with us?

331
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:38,542
When did he bring out his stand?

332
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:40,921
I'll give you a chance to rethink
